Adds the phase-5 acceptance regression canary and records the static
audit results for the phlink fork.

Tests
-----
* `PhlinkAdblockBundledRulesTest.BlocksTenSpotCheckHosts` —
  spans EasyList (doubleclick), Google AdSense / AdManager
  (pagead2.googlesyndication.com, securepubads.g.doubleclick.net,
  googletagservices.com, adservice.google.com), EasyPrivacy /
  analytics (google-analytics.com, googletagmanager.com,
  stats.g.doubleclick.net), and Facebook tracking
  (facebook.com/tr, connect.facebook.net/fbevents.js). All 10 must
  block; if any one stops blocking the bundled-list snapshot has
  regressed and 5-04 needs to be re-pinned.

  14/14 unit tests pass.

Audit (recorded in plan 5-08, not new code)
-------------------------------------------
* Netcap: `grep -rn 'googleapis\.com' chrome/browser/phlink/
  chrome/renderer/phlink/ third_party/phlink_filter_lists/` ⇒ only
  filter-list rules (which BLOCK phone-home traffic; expected).
  Component-updater pin from 5-07 means the only remaining
  Chromium-side phone-home is now `updates.phlink.invalid` (DNS
  fail-closed).
* Branding: `grep -rEn '"(Chrome|Chromium)"' chrome/browser/phlink/
  chrome/renderer/phlink/` ⇒ no hits. phlink dirs are clean.
* Google services: no `safebrowsing|sync_server|widevine`
  references in phlink dirs. Site isolation untouched (PRD §10.1
  D-04).

Manual smoke (run separately on the linked Chrome.app)
------------------------------------------------------
* 5 ad-laden sites: cnn.com, theguardian.com, forbes.com,
  weather.com, ndtv.com (visual confirmation that ads + cookie
  banners are gone, no console JS errors from missing trackers).
* `chrome://components` enumerates components (no crashes from the
  pinned updater URL).
* Cosmetic filtering renders correctly on a hand-crafted local
  test page (5-05 acceptance).
These remain user-driven gates; this commit covers the parts that
can be regressed by code changes alone.

Refs PRD §6 / §9 / §10.1 (D-05), plan 5-08.
